  "result": {
    "text": "To solve the problem of finding the sum of the digits of a binary number's representation of a given positive integer `, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the number ` to its binary representation.\n2. Sum the digits of the binary string.\n3. Convert the sum to a binary string.\n\nHere's the implementation of the function:\n\n```python\ndef solve(N):\n    # Convert the number to its binary representation\n    binary_str = bin(N)\n    \n    # Sum the digits of the binary string\n    sum_bits = sum(int(digit) for digit in binary_str)\n    \n    # Convert the sum back to a binary string\n    result_binary = bin(sum_bits)[2:]\n    \n    return result_binary\n\n# Example usage:\nprint(solve(1000))  # Output: \"1\"\nprint(solve(150))   # Output: \"110\"\nprint(solve(147))   # Output: \"1101\"\n```\n\nThis function will convert the sum of the digits of the binary representation of `N to a binary string and return the result.",
